<title>FRANCE: Renault sees investment slowing.</title>
<headline>Renault sees investment slowing.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French carmaker Renault SA said on Thursday its investments totalled 16.39 billion francs last year, around nine percent of sales, but expects that proportion to ease in coming years to between six and seven percent.</p>
<p>Chairman Louis Schweitzer said last year's investment, up from 15.26 billion francs in 1995, marked the end of a surge related to product renewals. &quot;We expect to bring it (investment) to six to seven percent of sales,&quot; he told reporters at a briefing on the carmaker's 1996 results.</p>
<p>(( --Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452))</p>
